# pick returns its own closure or, by a tail call, doubled's; doubled
# returns only its own. A tail call gives its caller's results, so the
# closures doubled returns are the ones pick returns, and nothing converts
# one after the call: it is a tail call from the program's first-order
# form on. Each calls the other, so neither is inlined into the other, and
# each is called from main as well, so each returns to more than one place
# and stays a function. pick may crash, so no copy of either takes in what
# its caller does with the closure.
first: tail-calls=@Main.pick:@Main.doubled
